@@ -8,6 +8,24 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates tool input against the declared `inputSchema` before invoking the executor.
+  A schema validation failure returns a `ToolResponse` with a description of the failure, allowing the provider to
+  retry the tool call on the next round within the `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` budget, instead of throwing and
+  ending the conversation. Executors no longer need to hand-validate their input; the contract now guarantees
+  input matching the declared schema reaches the executor.
+
+### Deprecated
+
+- Executors that relied on receiving malformed input to produce custom error messages no longer receive that input;
+  validation errors are now handled by the registry.
+
+### Changed
+
+- **MINOR version bump**: executors now receive only input that passes the schema, so tools that check `input.field !== undefined`
+  or cast defensively (`(input.field as Type)`) can remove this defensive logic.
+
